# EigenScript gap (an instance of no-int64): Lua 5.4 runs an integer 'for'
# a precomputed number of times (lvm.c forprep), so
#   for i = math.maxinteger - 1, math.maxinteger do ... end
# runs twice. With no 64-bit integer both bounds are the same double, 2^63:
# not an integer in [-2^63, 2^63), so the loop is a float loop whose step
# is absorbed (2^63 + 1 == 2^63) and it never ends (the corpus probe stops
# it after 5 rounds). Near mininteger the bounds also collapse: one round.
# Lua:  2 rounds near maxinteger, 2 near mininteger.
# Expected: false (the two bounds differ), then true.
# Actual 686d3b7d: true (they are equal), true.
# Rows: none graded (found by the round-3 critic).
mx is 9223372036854775807
print of (mx - 1 == mx)
print of (mx + 1 == mx)
